ow, but if I discard T4, maybe someone else can use it. \n\nAlternatively, W3 is part of a possible chow if there's a W2 and W4. But I don't have W2. \n\nGiven that, I'll go with discarding B7, as it's a single and already part of a completed meld by the player across. So the action would be Play B7.\n", "output": "Evaluation: The hand has three chows (W7-8-9, T2-3-4, B2-3-4) but lacks a fourth meld and a pair. Discarding B7 or B9 could allow forming a pair with remaining tiles, but no valid pair exists. The best move is to discard a tile that is part of a less critical sequence or a single to reduce the hand's vulnerability.\nReason: B7 is a single tile in the hand and is part of a completed meld (B5-6-7) by the player across, making it a safe discard. This minimizes the risk of others using it while maintaining potential for future melds.\nAnswer: Play B7"}
